     "style": "retenir",
     "title": "Dire l'heure",
     "md": "- **at six o'clock** : à six heures pile\n- **at half past seven** : à sept heures et demie\n- **at a quarter past eight** : à huit heures et quart\n- **in the morning / in the afternoon / in the evening / at night**\n\n*I have lunch at one o'clock in the afternoon.*"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 1 : raconter",
     "statement": "Raconte : Ngono se lève à 6 heures et va à l'école à 7 heures et demie.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Le sujet est Ngono : **she** → verbes avec -s."
      },
      {
       "md": "get up → **gets up** ; go → **goes**."
      },
      {
       "md": "*Ngono gets up at six o'clock. She goes to school at half past seven.*"
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**Ngono gets up at six o'clock. She goes to school at half past seven.**"
    },
    {
     "type": "example",
     "title": "Exemple 2 : poser une question",
     "statement": "Demande à un camarade à quelle heure il se lève.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "md": "Question au present simple : **What time** + do + sujet + verbe ?"
      },
      {
       "md": "Avec you : *What time do you get up ?*"
      },
      {
       "md": "Il répond : *I get up at six.*"
      }
     ],
     "answer": "**What time do you get up ?**"
    },
